From f294307a559a6fc565017baa493f89ee580f31c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:27:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(sim): the lathe field sweeps the blade's own
 meridian profile

A turning op now cuts the stock field with its tool's true footprint
instead of refusing blades by name (LATHE_BLADE_REFUSAL is gone):

- stock_sim::LatheProfile (new field_blade.rs): Nose (the existing
  stadium, unchanged closed form), Blade (grooving/parting rectangle of
  its width, corners rounded by corner_r), Thread (the V of its included
  angle cut off at the crest width), Form (the crown arc across its
  band, chorded inside the arc within CROWN_SAG_TOL = 1e-4 mm).
- The sweep of the convex footprint along a chord is the hull of both
  end copies; its signed distance is closed form, read in the query's
  meridian at both signs of the radius (parting past centre included).
- One reading with #103's meridian rapid law: tip at the band's centre,
  body outward by the tool's flute_len, V widening by tan(angle/2).
- Stock::simulate_lathe_profile; simulate_lathe(_about) delegate to the
  nose profile. The lathe entry points moved from backend.rs to
  field_lathe.rs (400-line law). LathePlan carries the profile; its
  display feature is the nose or half the blade's band.

Pinned by stock_lathe_blade (brute-force stamp reference at cell/20
steps: never under-cut, agreement within one step, for a corner-rounded
plunge groove, a part-off past centre, a two-pass 60-degree thread and a
form sink; nonsense profiles refused by name) and lathe_field_sim's
a_grooving_blade_cuts_its_rectangle_and_the_verdict_refuses_the_lathe
(a generated GrooveRough with zero sign misses against the swept
rectangle). No golden changed.

Fixes #21

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
